# Phase 4, Part B chunk B6: no code may write the job tables except the job store (internal/jobs). The fault adds a second non-test Go file under internal/jobengine/ that holds a raw string with an
# UPDATE platform.jobs SET status (the engine moving a job itself, past the lifecycle settings, the user's scope and the store's transaction); the gate must name the file and the line and say it is
# outside the sanctioned writer. The control side is the real repository, which must be green. Needs bash only: no database, no module, no Go.
# The patch adds a new file, so it depends on no committed file; the control needs internal/jobs/ (the store), scripts/check-job-writers.sh and tests/job-writer-exceptions.txt at HEAD.
GATE=job-writer
TARGET=platform
SETUP=
STEP=check-job-writers on the real repository
CMD=bash scripts/check-job-writers.sh
MESSAGE=internal/jobengine/zz_job_writer.go:4: write to platform.jobs (UPDATE) outside the sanctioned writer internal/jobs/
MESSAGE=check-job-writers: RED
